A few questions/spoilers:


1) I've noticed that an uncursed bag of holding makes things inside it
lighter (or weightless?) so you can carry lots in it.  And a cursed
bag of holding makes things inside it heavier, but has negative weight
(or makes things outside it lighter?) so you can carry lots of stuff
besides the bag.  (My current character has stumbled across not one,
but two ghost stacks containing cursed bags of holding.)  Does a
blessed bag of holding have any special properties, or does it act
like an uncursed one?

2) I was under the impression that eating tengus was a safe way to get
intrinsic teleport control and teleport, because you would get teleport
control first, then teleport.  But then last night Wally the Wizard ate
a tengu, and he got intrinsic teleport but not teleport control, so he
was jumping all over the place.  Luckily a ring of teleport control
turned up fairly quickly.  Is there a safe way to get teleport and
teleport control without a ring?

3) I know that giving money to a like-aligned priest is good: it
either decreases your armor class or gives you more luck.  But what
about non-like-aligned priests?  My neutral Wizard gave 400*level gold
to a lawful priest, and his armor class went way down.  Is there a
downside to this?


